From 43e8e6aab2d1367029e92729af0a3932bb3480c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bench <bench@local>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:36:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] null patch: 73-remove-dead-own-id-push-skip

push_pass skipped a pusher carrying the bot's own server id and let each id push once per pass (a HashSet built per bot per pass). That code could only act when one world holds two entities with one id, or an entity with the bot's own id. add_entity returns early for a known id, each join builds a new World, and the own id is registered only at login, so no packet reaches that state. Since patch 59 each bot has its own world, so the shared-world case it was written for is gone too. Removed own_id, mcid, the claimed set and the skip.

The only test that reached it, test_no_push_from_an_entity_with_the_bots_own_id, inserted the id by hand (entity_mut(other).insert(own)), which no packet can do. Removed with the code (entity_pushes tests 17 -> 16, azalea-client main 110 -> 109).

Vanilla: LivingEntity#pushEntities takes its candidates from Level#getEntities(this, ..), which leaves the entity itself out; one entity per id holds by construction in one level.
